resume: Following Kä Mana, the world of experience is the phenomenal world. Africans knew that life is terrible, inexplicable and dangerous, yet did not surrender to pessimism. African people must say “yes” to the world as an aesthetic phenomenon — in two ways, corresponding to the Dionysian and Apollonian attitudes.
